From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mark Harfouche <mark.harfouche@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 08:38:22 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Windows runtime support from triton-windows

Taken from https://github.com/triton-lang/triton-windows (v3.9.0-windows.post30):
runtime/build.py (MSVC, clang-cl and bundled TinyCC compilers),
windows_utils.py (MSVC/Windows SDK/CUDA/Python discovery), cache.py,
driver.py, the NVIDIA launcher (nvcuda.dll via LoadLibrary, aligned
allocation, TinyCC-compatible initializers) and named pipes for the
warmup pool. The gcc/clang command line on non-Windows is kept as
upstream.
